{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The driver asked the rider to cancel, and the chat log proves it on its face. MSG-02733-001, sent by the DRIVER at 2026-08-15T07:52:21+08:00 and read by the rider at 07:52:51, says 'sorry got a problem with the car, can you cancel on your side'. The rider replied 'ok cancelling' at 07:53:21 (MSG-02733-002) and the trip was cancelled by the rider at 07:55:21. That is squarely the third exception in POL-NS-10(f) - the driver asked the rider to cancel, and the chat_log shows it. The $4.50 cancellation fee must therefore be refunded to the rider in full, and the rider's own cancellation stops being the operative fact.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02733", "EV-TRIP-02733"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-10"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The charge is labelled a no-show fee, but no limb of POL-NS-01 holds on this record. The trip record's event chain runs driver_assigned 07:48:21, driver_en_route 07:48:29, trip_cancelled 07:55:21 - there is no driver 'arrived' event anywhere, so limb (a) fails. The driver's own trace then breaks limb (b): across 49 fixes the driver is never once inside the pickup geofence, and the qualifying in-radius fix count is zero. Where the anchor clause fails, the fee is not chargeable under it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02733", "EV-GPS-02733"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Limb (d) of POL-NS-01 independently fails. The record shows no boarding event and the trip was terminated with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_CANCELLED - not RIDER_NO_SHOW, not RIDER_UNREACHABLE, not EXCESSIVE_WAIT. A no-show fee cannot be built on a cancellation recorded under the rider's ordinary cancellation code; the mis-selected code is a driver-education item, not a basis for keeping the fee.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02733"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-02 deems a driver arrived only where at least 3 consecutive fixes, each accurate to 25 m or better, fall inside the arrival radius - 50 m for this STANDARD zone class, read from the fee schedule. The driver's trace carries 49 fixes over the window, zero qualifying in-radius fixes, and a minimum distance to the pickup pin of 7000.03 m: the closest he ever came was seven kilometres away. On this trace the driver never arrived, limb (b) of POL-NS-01 fails, and the rider is entitled to a full refund of the cancellation fee.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02733", "EV-TRIP-02733"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The softer wrong-entrance route cannot rescue this fee either. POL-NS-03 exists for a driver stationary outside the arrival radius but not more than 400 m from the pin; here the driver's minimum distance was 7.0 km, more than seventeen times that ceiling, so the clause is never engaged and nothing about fault allocation between the parties can displace the refund that POL-NS-02 gives the rider.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02733", "EV-TRIP-02733"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The effective in-geofence dwell is zero seconds against the 180 second free waiting period in force for this trip (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec, STANDARD zone) - a shortfall of 180 seconds, with a longest qualifying run of 0 fixes. The driver's recorded speeds across the trace run from 57.2 to 62.9 km/h, which is a driver moving on a road, not a driver holding position at a pickup. Nor can he accumulate dwell: POL-NS-06(i) requires a present, populated traffic_advisory of type KERB_RESTRICTION, ENFORCEMENT, CLOSURE or ACCIDENT, and EV-ADVIS-02733-01 is MISSING (an absent artifact, weight 0.0, which I disclose), so limb (i) is unavailable by its own terms and a MISSING advisory can never reduce the minimum. The full refund stands and no driver compensation is payable.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02733", "EV-TRIP-02733", "EV-ADVIS-02733-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.shortfall_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Every artifact this case turns on is clean, so there is no impairment discount. The fare_breakdown cancellation-fee line is 4.50 and reconciles with platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd of 4.50, so POL-NS-08(d) is not met; the chat carries 2 messages matching trip_record.chat_message_count of 2 with sequence numbering intact, so limb (c) is not met; the trace reports 100.0% coverage at a 10 second cadence with max_gap_sec 0.0, so limb (b) is not met; and the trip record's timestamps align with the trace, so limb (a) is not met. The facts that decide this dispute are carried by artifacts at weight multiplier 1.0 and there is no ground to down-weight them.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02733", "EV-CHAT-02733", "EV-GPS-02733", "EV-TRIP-02733"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No escalation trigger fires, so this dispute should be decided on the merits as a full refund rather than held in human review. rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1, below the 3 that POL-NS-09(d) requires; disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0 on both profiles, so limb (c) does not fire; and driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 0 against completed_trips_30d of 55, so the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check (4 or more terminations and a rate above 0.08) does not trip. With admissible, complete evidence and no abuse signal on either side, the fee should be returned to the rider now.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-02733", "EV-DPROF-02733"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09", "POL-NS-07"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

