    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "The $4.50 cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-02733 is refunded to the rider in full.\n\nFor the driver: your case starts from a correct proposition. The rider cancelled the trip herself at 07:55:21, 420 seconds after the 07:48:21 acceptance, so the 180-second grace in trip_record.platform_policy.grace_after_match_sec had expired, and under POL-NS-10(f) a rider's own post-grace cancellation is chargeable at platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd ($4.50 on this record) whether or not you had arrived. But the same limb of the same clause refunds the fee in full where the chat_log shows the driver asked the rider to cancel, and that is exactly what this record shows: MSG-02733-001, sent by you at 07:52:21 and read at 07:52:51, reads 'sorry got a problem with the car, can you cancel on your side', and the rider replied 'ok cancelling' at 07:53:21 (MSG-02733-002). Your own advocate concedes the point. Your ETA argument does not rescue the fee: the exception turns on your request, not on whether you were running late, and in any event the rider cancelled roughly eight minutes before the 08:03 arrival time quoted to her. Your point that the fare ledger is clean is accepted (fare_breakdown.cancellation_fee $4.50 equals platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd $4.50, and EV-FARE-02733 is COMPLETE at weight 1.0), but a correctly computed amount is not a chargeable one.\n\nIndependently, the no-show foundation fails and would give the rider the same refund. POL-NS-01 requires a driver 'arrived' event (the trip record has none - its event chain is driver_assigned, driver_en_route, trip_cancelled), fixes inside the pickup geofence (the driver's closest approach to the pin is 7,000.03 m, and across 49 fixes he holds 57.2-62.9 km/h with 0 qualifying in-geofence fixes), and a termination under RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE or EXCESSIVE_WAIT (the record shows RIDER_CANCELLED). POL-NS-02 accordingly also entitles the rider to the full fee back, and POL-NS-03 is not engaged because 7.0 km is far beyond its 400 m ceiling.\n\nFor the rider: your claims are accepted. The driver's request to cancel is decisive under POL-NS-10(f); the driver never arrived (limbs (a), (b) and (d) of POL-NS-01 all fail); POL-NS-04 need not exonerate you because you win on POL-NS-10(f) regardless; and every artifact this ruling rests on is COMPLETE at weight 1.0, so there is no impairment discount. The one absent artifact, EV-ADVIS-02733-01 (TRAFFIC_ADVISORY, MISSING, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT), carries no fact here and is not relied on: no advisory covers Blk 231 Serangoon Ave 3, so POL-NS-06(i) dwell aggregation is unavailable, but the refund does not depend on it.\n\nAmount and compensation: $4.50 is refunded, being the contested cancellation-fee line of EV-FARE-02733 and matching platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd; no waiting-time fee was charged (waiting_time_fee $0.00) and none is due, since POL-NS-10(d) bars charging both on one trip. No driver compensation is payable: POL-NS-07 pays the driver only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and it is not, so the anti-farming check never comes into play.\n\nNo escalation: POL-NS-09 is not triggered - rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1 (below 3), disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0 on both profiles, and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming test does not trip - and confidence is above the 0.70 floor. The monetary effect ($4.50) is below the $8.00 execution threshold, so this refund executes automatically."
  },
