    "explanation": "Rider and driver: the $4.50 cancellation fee charged on TRP-02733 is refunded in full to the rider. The charge stands or falls under POL-NS-10, the only clause that decides a fee a rider's own cancellation triggers, and its limb (f) refunds the fee in full where the chat log shows the driver asked the rider to cancel. It does: MSG-02733-001, sent by the DRIVER at 07:52:21, reads 'sorry got a problem with the car, can you cancel on your side', and the rider's MSG-02733-002 at 07:53:21 answers 'ok cancelling'. She cancelled at 07:55:21 — 420 seconds after acceptance, past the 180-second grace_after_match_sec in force — so the fee would prima facie be chargeable under POL-NS-10(f), but the driver-requested-cancellation exception applies and the fee is refunded in full. The DRIVER advocate's own framing is accepted: this was a rider-triggered, post-grace cancellation rather than a driver-terminated no-show, and the refund runs to the cancellation-fee line of $4.50 only. No waiting-time fee was charged (waiting_time_fee $0.00) and POL-NS-10(d) bars both on one trip, so nothing beyond $4.50 is returnable. The no-show anchor fails independently as well: POL-NS-01 needs a driver 'arrived' event (none exists), in-geofence presence (the driver's trace carries 0 qualifying in-radius fixes, closest approach 7,000.03 m from the pin) and a termination under RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE or EXCESSIVE_WAIT — the record reads RIDER_CANCELLED. POL-NS-02 confirms the driver never arrived, and POL-NS-03 never engages (its 400 m ceiling is exceeded many times over). I do not accept the rider's rider-education suggestion of a mis-selected reason code: the rider cancelled her own trip and RIDER_CANCELLED is the correct code for that, so no clause produces a referral on these facts. On the remaining points: the fare ledger is clean — $4.50 equals platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd and reconciles to total_charged, so POL-NS-08(d) is not met and there is no basis to reduce the amount; POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider (her only message 'ok cancelling' identifies no location, and her single rider-track fix at 07:57:11 postdates the cancellation), but that does not matter because the refund comes from POL-NS-10(f), not POL-NS-04; POL-NS-06's dwell arithmetic is not the operative test on a rider-cancelled trip and the driver claims nothing under its limb (i). No escalation trigger fires: confidence is above the 0.70 floor; both tracks and the ledger are COMPLETE at weight 1.0 with no contradiction; disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0 on both profiles; rider no_show_disputes_30d is 1 (below 3); and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d 0, rate 0.0). Every artifact carrying the deciding facts — the chat log, the trip record and the GPS trace — is at weight 1.0; the only impaired artifact is the MISSING traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02733-01 at weight 0.0, which carries no fact this ruling rests on. The $4.50 refund is below the $8.00 execution threshold and executes automatically."
