    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Rider and driver: the $4.50 cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-02733 (EV-FARE-02733, cancellation_fee $4.50, total_charged $4.50, payment_status CHARGED) is refunded to the rider in full.\n\nWhat the record shows. The driver accepted the job at 07:48:21 and set off; at 07:52:21 he messaged the rider, \"sorry got a problem with the car, can you cancel on your side\" (MSG-02733-001, EV-CHAT-02733, read by the rider at 07:52:51). The rider replied \"ok cancelling\" at 07:53:21 and cancelled the trip at 07:55:21 (EV-TRIP-02733, cancelled_by RIDER, reason code RIDER_CANCELLED).\n\nThe driver's position, accepted. The driver is right that this was a rider-triggered cancellation made 420 seconds after acceptance, beyond the 180-second grace in trip_record.platform_policy.grace_after_match_sec, and that under POL-NS-10(f) such a cancellation is chargeable at platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd, $4.50, \"whether or not the driver had arrived\". He is also right that the fare ledger is clean: $4.50 equals platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd, so no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect exists, and his point that the ETA exception is not engaged (the driver was still moving at 57.2-62.9 km/h when the rider cancelled) is accepted.\n\nBut POL-NS-10(f) carries a further exception, and it decides the case: the fee \"is refunded in full where the record shows ... the driver asked the rider to cancel (chat_log)\". The chat log shows exactly that, in the driver's own words and timestamp. The driver's advocate concedes this on the record. The refund therefore follows, and it is a full refund of the cancellation-fee line.\n\nThe rider's no-show route, accepted as far as it goes but not the operative ground. The rider is right that the charge cannot be sustained as a no-show fee: there is no 'arrived' event and no boarding event in the trip record, the termination is recorded as CANCELLED_BY_RIDER / RIDER_CANCELLED rather than a no-show code, so POL-NS-01 limbs (a) and (d) fail; and the driver's own trace carries 0 qualifying in-geofence fixes with a minimum distance of 7,000.03 m (7.0 km) across 49 fixes, so POL-NS-02 finds no arrival and POL-NS-01 limb (b) fails. POL-NS-03 does not change this: it engages only within 400 m of the pin, and the closest the driver came was 7.0 km, so no wrong-entrance outcome - and no POL-NS-03(ii) pin-ambiguity goodwill - is available. These clauses point the same way as POL-NS-10(f); the fee is refunded because the driver asked for the cancellation, and would also fail as a no-show charge in any event.\n\nClaims that do not move the outcome. POL-NS-04 is not needed: the rider's \"ok cancelling\" message is not a locating or coordinating message and her single rider fix is timed 07:57:11, after the 07:55:21 cancellation, so that clause would not exonerate her on its own tests - but the refund does not depend on it. The POL-NS-06 dwell arithmetic likewise decides nothing here: the disputed $4.50 is a cancellation fee on a rider-cancelled trip, decided under POL-NS-10.\n\nDriver compensation. None is payable. POL-NS-10(f) is a full refund of the fee and carries no driver payment, and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming test is not reached because POL-NS-01 is not satisfied; the POL-NS-03(ii) goodwill route is unavailable for the distance reason above.\n\nEscalation and referrals. No POL-NS-09 trigger fires: disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0 on both profiles (limb (c)), rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1 against the 3 limb (d) requires, the anti-farming check reads driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d = 0 against completed_trips_30d = 55 (limb (d)), no two admissible artifacts contradict each other (limb (b)), and the deciding fact is not carried solely by an impaired artifact (limb (e)). No clause produces a referral: no arrival marker was tapped, so POL-NS-05(ii)'s false-arrival record does not fire, and POL-NS-01's driver-education referral is confined to a mis-selected reason code on an in-radius arrival, which is not this case. The reason code RIDER_CANCELLED correctly describes a rider cancellation.\n\nImpairment and confidence. EV-ADVIS-02733-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT); this ruling does not rely on it. The rider's POL-NS-06 dwell claim, which cited that missing artifact without naming its issue code, was discarded at the mechanical check and supports nothing. The deciding fact - that the driver asked the rider to cancel - is carried by the chat log EV-CHAT-02733 at weight 1.0, and the amount by the fare breakdown EV-FARE-02733 at weight 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0 and confidence is 0.95, above the 0.70 policy floor. The monetary effect of $4.50 does not exceed the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of $8.00, so it executes automatically. This is a provisional ruling and either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04."
  },
